@startuml sequence_env_install
!theme plain
' Compact layout (tuned per diagram — see README, 'Sequence-diagram layout').
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 140
skinparam wrapWidth 200
title Dependency Install — Setup -> Advanced (gated)

actor User
participant "Setup -> Advanced\n(Streamlit)" as Adv
participant "api_client\n(httpx)" as Client
participant "FastAPI\n/app.py" as API
participant "install_jobs.py\n(job manager)" as Jobs
participant "pip / git\n(subprocess)" as Proc
participant "install.log" as Log

note over Adv, API: Tab shown only if /health advanced_enabled (DEAP_ENABLE_ADVANCED)

== Start install ==
User -> Adv: choose op (pip install | pip uninstall | git clone)\n+ package/URL -> "Run"
Adv -> Client: POST /env/install {manager, action, args}
Client -> API: HTTP POST
API -> API: _require_advanced() (else 403)
API -> Jobs: start_install(manager, action, args)
Jobs -> Jobs: build_command(...)\nallowlist + reject metacharacters
note right of Jobs: InstallValidationError -> 400
Jobs -> Proc: create_subprocess_exec(\n  [python -m pip ...] | [git clone --depth 1 ...],\n  stdout=install.log)
Jobs -> Jobs: create_task(_await_proc)\n(track {job_id: proc})
Jobs --> API: job_id
API --> Client: 201 {job_id, status:"running"}
Client --> Adv: store job_id in session_state

== Poll output (st.fragment run_every=2s) ==
loop until status != running
    Adv -> Client: GET /env/install/{job_id}?lines=300
    Client -> API: HTTP GET
    API -> Jobs: get_status(job_id, lines)
    Jobs -> Log: read_tail(...)
    Jobs --> API: {status, returncode, command, text, ...}
    API --> Client: InstallStatusResponse
    Client --> Adv: render command + 🔄/✅/❌ badge + st.code(log)
end

Proc --> Jobs: exit code -> status completed/failed

note over Adv
  Container caveat: installs land in the backend
  container's site-packages and are LOST on rebuild.
  Add permanent deps to Dockerfile.server.
end note

@enduml
